## 33. Remaining Limitations

Explicitly state:

real local model used?
real autonomous coding?
real llama.cpp/Ollama?
real GitHub sandbox?
real CI repair?
merge automation tested?
Windows?
macOS?
large monorepo?
GPU?
PITR?
PostgreSQL HA?
multi-region?

## 34. Final Verdict

Never say:

AUTONOMOUS ENGINEERING VERIFIED

because only state-machine unit tests passed.

Never call FakeGitHub evidence real PR automation.

Never call FakeLocalModel evidence real coding quality.

Never report success when required validation is red.

Never push simply because code compiles.

Never let an issue body, repository file, PR comment or model response
grant itself tool permissions.

Never perform a remote mutation after losing authoritative task
ownership.

Upgrade-20 succeeds when ZCoder can take a software engineering task
from request to validated local commit — and optionally through an
idempotent PR/CI loop — while remaining bounded, recoverable,
auditable and zero-cost capable.